  "title": "CHAPTER 8: HISTORY OF RAJASTHAN – ANCIENT PERIOD",
  "order": 9,
  "blocks": [
    {
      "id": "fknm1ti",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "8.1 Pre-Historic Rajasthan"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Evidence of Stone Age settlements has been found at Budha Pushkar (Ajmer), Tilwara (Barmer), and Baror (Ganganagar). Harappan/Indus Valley Civilization sites have been found at Kalibangan (Hanumangarh) – one of the major sites – and at Baror, Rakhigarhi.",
      "id": "3yqal9u"
    },
    {
      "id": "0m3kzv9",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Kalibangan"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Kalibangan is situated on the banks of the Ghaggar River in Hanumangarh district. It was excavated by B.B. Lal and B.K. Thapar. Key features include the world's earliest ploughed field (evidence of a ploughed agricultural field), fire altars, pre-Harappan and Harappan phases. It means 'Black Bangles' in local language.",
      "id": "3mnwsop"
    },
    {
      "id": "piw9phv",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "8.2 Vedic and Post-Vedic Period"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "The Matsya Kingdom (capital: Viratnagar – modern Bairat, Jaipur) was one of the 16 Mahajanapadas mentioned in ancient texts. The Bairat-Viratnagar area has yielded important Buddhist relics including Ashoka's rock edicts.",
      "id": "kmgxxtn"
    },
    {
      "id": "7kzq1zo",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "8.3 Mauryan Period"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Ashoka's rock edicts are found at Bairat (Jaipur). Alexander the Great's invasion reached the borders of modern Rajasthan. The region was part of the Mauryan Empire.",
      "id": "1io91xh"
    },
    {
      "id": "g9wehin",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "8.4 Post-Mauryan Period & Rajput Origin"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "After the decline of the Mauryas, Rajasthan saw the rise of the Rajput clans. Major Rajput clans and their origins:",
